// [ORG] Possible C2 beaconing - rare public destination contacted persistently by few devices
// Platform : Defender XDR custom detection (Advanced Hunting)   Version 1.0 (promoted from hunt.kql)
// Frequency: Every hour  ->  platform lookback 4 h, evaluated on ingestion_time()  (fixed pair for XDR data)
// Severity : Medium      MITRE: TA0011 Command and Control / T1071 Application Layer Protocol
//            (the predicate asserts regular, persistent egress from one device to a rare public IP;
//             it does not assert the protocol, so T1071 is the closest behaviour-level technique)
//
// DETECTION STRATEGY: a compromised device talks to its C2 on a sleep timer, so a single public IP
//   that is contacted repeatedly across the whole lookback window by only a handful of devices is
//   the cheapest observable shape of beaconing.
// THE MECHANIC: implant sleeps N seconds, wakes, completes a TCP connection (ConnectionSuccess), repeats.
// THE RESILIENCE: keyed on DeviceId + RemoteIP. The initiating process is context only - renamed or
//   injected implants change the process name, not the destination or the cadence.
// DATA: DeviceNetworkEvents / ActionType == "ConnectionSuccess" (MDE). Network telemetry is THROTTLED
//   by the sensor (sampled: yes) -> counts can be undercounted; expect false negatives, never inflation.
// TP LIKELIHOOD WHEN IT FIRES: medium - benign polling agents (monitoring, licence, update, chat and
//   telemetry clients) produce the same shape; precision comes from the population filter and the
//   environment-specific tuning region below.   COVERAGE CAVEAT: sleeps longer than ~15 min, beacons
//   spread over more than MaxDevices hosts, and beacons that stop within the window are not caught.
// ANALYST ACTION: pivot on RemoteIP (reputation, passive DNS, which other devices ever touched it),
//   then on InitiatingProcessSHA256 (FileProfile prevalence / signer) and the Processes set.
//
// WINDOW CONTRACT: the service pre-filters EVERY table reference in a custom detection to the lookback
//   (hourly => 4 h) on ingestion_time(); results outside it are ignored. Therefore this rule carries
//   NO Timestamp/ingestion_time() filter of its own (a Timestamp filter would drop late-arriving events),
//   and every threshold below is expressed relative to a 4 h window - NOT the hunt's 7 d / 12 h.
//   First run after save scans 30 days: expect a one-off burst (see promotion-notes.md).
let query_frequency = 1h;   // == rule frequency in the portal ("Every hour")
let query_period    = 4h;   // == fixed XDR lookback for an hourly rule; applied by the platform, mirrored here for reviewers
let BinSize         = 30m;  // persistence grain: 4 h / 30 m = 8 bins per window
// --- Tunables (each states its meaning and the FP it trades against) ---
let MaxDevices     = 3;     // population filter: RemoteIP seen by more devices in the window is shared infra (SaaS, CDN, update) -> not rare.
                            //   Raising it admits more shared services (FPs); lowering it misses beacons spread over several compromised hosts (blind spot).
let MinConnections = 16;    // per DeviceId+RemoteIP in 4 h  ~ one connection every 15 min. Hunt had no floor (it ranked). Lower -> slower sleeps caught, more chatty-but-benign clients alerted.
let MinActiveBins  = 6;     // of 8 half-hour bins must contain traffic (>= 75 % of the window). Replaces the hunt's "span > 12 h": a burst of 16 downloads in one
                            //   bin, or two connections 3 h apart, must NOT satisfy persistence. Lower -> catches intermittent beacons, admits bursty transfers.
let MinSpanMinutes = 180;   // first-to-last connection must span >= 3 h of the 4 h window (the hunt's 12 h-of-7 d criterion, rescaled). Keeps short sessions out.
// --- Stage 1: collapse to the investigated entity pair (device <-> destination) inside the lookback ---
let Pairs = materialize(          // referenced twice (population filter + alert set)
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where ActionType == "ConnectionSuccess" and RemoteIPType == "Public"
| where isnotempty(RemoteIP)
// Begin environment-specific filter.
// OPTION: exclude corporate egress / SaaS / vendor ranges (hoist to a let KnownGoodRanges = dynamic([...]) or a watchlist on the Sentinel variant):
//         | where not(ipv4_is_in_any_range(RemoteIP, KnownGoodRanges))      // blind spot: C2 hosted inside an excluded range will not fire
// OPTION: exclude known polling agents by SIGNER/product, never by file name (renamed binaries):
//         | where InitiatingProcessVersionInfoCompanyName !in~ (KnownPollingVendors)  // blind spot: C2 injected into / impersonating that vendor's process
// OPTION: tighten to bare-IP destinations (most C2 is IP-only; most SaaS has a hostname):  | where isempty(RemoteUrl)   // blind spot: domain-fronted / DNS-resolved C2
// OPTION: exclude proxies, scanners and internet-facing servers whose fan-out is their job: | where DeviceId !in (HighFanOutDevices)
// End environment-specific filter.
| summarize hint.shufflekey = RemoteIP
    (Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessSHA256) =
        arg_max(Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessSHA256),   // latest event carries the XDR contract columns
    Connections  = count(),
    FirstSeen    = min(Timestamp),
    LastSeen     = max(Timestamp),
    ActiveBins   = dcount(bin(Timestamp, BinSize)),
    Processes    = make_set(InitiatingProcessFileName, 10),   // capped: the hunt's unbounded make_set is a payload risk
    RemotePorts  = make_set(RemotePort, 10)
  by DeviceId, RemoteIP
);
// --- Stage 2: population filter - how many devices in the window touched each destination ---
let RareDestinations = Pairs
| summarize Devices = dcount(DeviceId) by RemoteIP
| where Devices <= MaxDevices;
// --- Stage 3: compound, floored thresholds on the pair; one row per DeviceId+RemoteIP ---
Pairs
| lookup kind=inner RareDestinations on RemoteIP          // small dimension set: lookup, not join
| extend SpanMinutes = datetime_diff('minute', LastSeen, FirstSeen)
| where Connections >= MinConnections
    and ActiveBins >= MinActiveBins
    and SpanMinutes >= MinSpanMinutes
| extend AvgIntervalSeconds = toint(datetime_diff('second', LastSeen, FirstSeen) / (Connections - 1))   // Connections >= MinConnections, so never /0
| project-reorder Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName, RemoteIP, RemotePorts, Devices, Connections, ActiveBins, SpanMinutes,
                  AvgIntervalSeconds, FirstSeen, LastSeen, InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessSHA256, Processes, ReportId
// XDR contract: Timestamp, ReportId, DeviceId, DeviceName present after the final operator.
// Impacted asset: Device (DeviceId). Related evidence: IP (RemoteIP), Process (InitiatingProcessFileName / InitiatingProcessSHA256).
// Custom details: Devices, Connections, ActiveBins, SpanMinutes, AvgIntervalSeconds, RemotePorts, Processes.
// DedupFields: DeviceId, RemoteIP - the platform collapses identical entity + custom-detail rows within a run and across the
//   4 h / 1 h lookback overlap. Re-validate this key whenever the projection changes.
